## Table of Contents
Hierarchically porous biocatalytic MOFs provide sufficient space for accommodated enzymes to reorientate and spread in their lower surface energy state as well to decrease the inherent barriers to accelerate the diffusion of reactants and intermediates. The promoted intermolecular correlation of enzymes and MOFs and polyphenol coating safeguard the enzymes from inactivation, showcasing their promise for diverse biotechnological applications.
